cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use the TIER-Graph API specification, please cite it as below."
title: "TIER-Graph API: An Implementation-Neutral Specification for Temporally Indexed, Evidence-Linked Derived Relations"
abstract: >-
  TIER-Graph (Temporally Indexed Evidence-Linked Relations Graph) is an
  implementation-neutral API specification for publishing, querying, and
  auditing derived relational propositions whose evidence is linked to
  externally controlled temporal source states through a declared grounding
  profile. The specification separates three ontological objects
  (DerivedEntity, DerivedRelation, RelationEvidence) from an external
  authoritative source substrate, and computes time-indexed evidential state
  from evidence admissibility rather than from copied source intervals.
type: software
authors:
